# Vue

- Vue 3 + TypeScript. `<script setup lang="ts">`. No Options API unless a file already uses it.
- Tailwind v4 only, **mobile-first**: unprefixed utilities = phone; `md:`/`lg:` = larger screens. Convert mockup look to utilities; do not paste Canvas inline CSS into Vue.
- Path aliases: `@/app`, `@/features`, `@/shared`.
- **PWA only if Aldrin said it is required.** Then add `vite-plugin-pwa`, web manifest (`display: standalone`, `theme-color`), 192 and 512 icons, offline fallback, `viewport-fit=cover` in `index.html`, and a root app shell whose fixed top/bottom chrome uses safe-area insets (see `ui-ux.mdc`). Until then, do not add a service worker — but still use safe-area-aware bottom/top padding on fixed nav when building mobile layouts (browser chrome overlaps the same way in the tab).

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { ref } from 'vue'
</script>
```

## Feature-based folders

Group by capability. Kebab-case feature names. Other features import only from `index.ts`.

```
src/
  app/
  features/<name>/
    components/
    views/
    stores/
    api.ts             # only network/fixture access
    fixtures.ts        # dev test data
    routes.ts
    types.ts
    index.ts
  shared/              # used by 2+ features only
    components/
    composables/
    api/               # shared HTTP wrapper if needed
    fixtures/
    assets/
  router/
```

Views talk to Pinia; Pinia talks to `api.ts`. No `fetch` in components. `api.ts` returns fixtures when `VITE_USE_FIXTURES === 'true'`, otherwise the real HTTP API.
